   [8x1]^+6 x1: Q = 1

=== B6. Does 144 contain a copy of the SM content of 16+ ? (multiset containment) ===
144+: max copies of SM(16+) contained = 0; of SM(16-) = 1
144-: max copies of SM(16+) contained = 1; of SM(16-) = 0

=== B8. Majorana-Weyl reading: left-handed spin-1/2 content of nu (+) zeta, nu in S+, zeta in T*(x)S- ===
left-handed spin-1/2 Spin(10) content: {'S+': 3, 'R-': 1}
max number of copies of the SM content of one generation (16+) contained: 4
remaining spin-1/2 states after removing them: 128
left-handed spin-3/2 [(3,2) x .] Spin(10) content of zeta: {'S-': 1}

=== B9. Reality readings: left-handed spin-1/2 Spin(10) content, net chirality #16+ - #16- ===
  Majorana-Weyl (real)   zeta in T*(x)(S-): LH spin-1/2 = {'R-': 1, 'S+': 3}; #16+ - #16- = 3; #144- - #144+ = 1
  Majorana-Weyl (real)   zeta in T*(x)(S+): LH spin-1/2 = {'R+': 1, 'S+': 1, 'S-': 2}; #16+ - #16- = -1; #144- - #144+ = -1
  complex Weyl           zeta in T*(x)(S-): LH spin-1/2 = {'R-': 2, 'S+': 6}; #16+ - #16- = 6; #144- - #144+ = 2
  complex Weyl           zeta in T*(x)(S+): LH spin-1/2 = {'R+': 2, 'S+': 2, 'S-': 4}; #16+ - #16- = -2; #144- - #144+ = -2
  Dirac (S+ + S-)        zeta in T*(x)(S++S-): LH spin-1/2 = {'R+': 2, 'R-': 2, 'S+': 6, 'S-': 6}; #16+ - #16- = 0; #144- - #144+ = 0

=== B7. Source formula (4.2): internal spinor dimension for normal bundle of rank n(n+1)/2 ===
n=2: rank N = 3 odd -> no Weyl splitting
n=3: rank N = 6, Dirac 2^(r/2) = 8, Weyl = 4; total dim Y = 9
n=4: rank N = 10, Dirac 2^(r/2) = 32, Weyl = 16; total dim Y = 14
n=5: rank N = 15 odd -> no Weyl splitting
n=6: rank N = 21 odd -> no Weyl splitting
n=7: rank N = 28, Dirac 2^(r/2) = 16384, Weyl = 8192; total dim Y = 35
n=8: rank N = 36, Dirac 2^(r/2) = 262144, Weyl = 131072; total dim Y = 44
